ong (armed, waiting for the trigger). Desk backtest for S1: edge (+0.07R over 3362 trades). Holmes weakness sequence W4 (no demand → upthrust → no demand) completed 9 Oct: no demand 2 Oct → upthrust 6 Oct → no demand 9 Oct. It confirms on a trade below 96.63; a close above 99.16 proves it wrong (armed, waiting for the trigger). Desk backtest for W4: negative (-0.11R over 9631 trades). Strength and weakness sequences disagree here, so the background decides; wait for the bar that confirms one of them."},"scores":{"overall":47,"group":"SIC 63 Insurance Carriers","group_rank":6,"group_n":41,"sector_rank":62,"sector_n":424,"earn":25}},"biz":{"name":"MetLife, Inc.","desc":"MetLife is one of the largest life insurers in the US by assets and provides a variety of life insurance and annuity products. It is organized into six segments: group benefits, retirement and income solutions, Asia, Latin America, Europe/Middle East/Africa (EMEA), and MetLife Investment Managenent. Group Benefits and RIS are US-based, contributing to around 52% of the firm's 2025 adjusted earnings. The Asia segment contributes around 25% of earnings, mainly tied to Japan. The company also holds leading market positions in Mexico and Chile, with the Latin America segment contributing around 14% of 2024 earnings. The EMEA and investment management segments contributed around 6% and 3% of 2025 earnings, respectively.","desc_src":"Massive (formerly Polygon.io) ticker details","sic":"6311","sic_desc":"Life Insurance","sector":"Financial Services","industry":"Insurance - Life","mcap":59957248062.45,"mcap_src":"Massive ticker details (2026-10-03)","shares":643436779,"shares_src":"Massive ticker details (share-class shares outstanding)","hq":"NEW YORK, NY","website":"https://www.metlife.com","employees":46000,"list_date":"2000-04-05","exchange":"XNYS","fy_end":"1231","cik":1099219,"state_inc":"DE","massive_asof":"2026-10-03","sec_asof":"2026-10-03"},"fin":{"available":true,"src":"SEC EDGAR XBRL companyfacts",